"file2.txt\"]\n      stdin: null\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout_structure: three lines — file1 counts, file2 counts, total with label \"total\"; columns right-aligned\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd005-wc R1.4\n      - prd005-wc R3.1\n      - prd005-wc R3.2\n\n  - name: wc_total_only\n    description: '--total=only with two files prints only the total line. Setup: file1.txt contains \"a\\n\", file2.txt contains \"b\\nc\\n\"'\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"--total=only\", \"file1.txt\", \"file2.txt\"]\n      stdin: null\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout_structure: one line with summed counts and label \"total\"\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd005-wc R3.3\n\n  - name: wc_total_never\n    description: '--total=never with two files prints no total line. Setup: file1.txt contains \"x\\n\", file2.txt contains \"y\\n\"'\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"--total=never\", \"file1.txt\", \"file2.txt\"]\n      stdin: null\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout_structure: two lines (one per file), no total line\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd005-wc R3.3\n\n  - name: wc_stdin_dash\n    description: '\"-\" as a filename argument reads from stdin.'\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"-\"]\n      stdin: \"stdin content\\n\"\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout_structure: one line of counts (no filename label for stdin dash)\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd005-wc R4.1\n\n  - name: wc_empty_stdin\n    description: Zero bytes of stdin produces \"0 0 0\" for default flags.\n    inputs:\n      args: []\n      stdin: \"\"\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout_structure: 'output contains \"0\"'\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd005-wc R4.3\n\n  - name: wc_missing_file\n    description: 'Non-existent file prints error to stderr, exits 1, processes remaining files. Setup: real.txt contains \"data\\n\", nonexistent.txt does not exist'\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"nonexistent.txt\", \"real.txt\"]\n      stdin: null\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 1\n      stdout_structure: counts for real.txt and a total line are printed\n      stderr_contains: \"nonexistent.txt\"\n    traces:\n      - prd005-wc R6.2\n","numLines":211,"startLine":1,"totalLines":211}}}
