{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01GuYxLs2uRwftnAxUvKDf83","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have a clear picture. Let me implement `cmd/wc/main.go`. Key requirements:\n\n- Count lines (`-l`), words (`-w`), bytes (`-c`), chars (`-m`), max line length (`-L`)\n- Default: lines, words, bytes\n- `-m` overrides `-c` when both given\n- Output order: lines, words, chars/bytes, max-line-length (fixed, regardless of flag order)\n- Multi-file: per-file + total line, right-aligned columns\n- `--total=auto|always|only|never`\n- `--files0-from=FILE`\n- `-` means stdin\n- Exit 0 on success, 1 on error\n- SIGPIPE handler\n- `LC_ALL=C` for tests\n\nLet me check how GNU wc formats its output — GNU wc uses a minimum field width based on the number of digits in the largest count. For single file/stdin with small counts, GNU wc uses a minimum width of 1 (no padding). For multiple files, it right-justifies to the width of the largest count.\n\nActually, looking at GNU wc more carefully: for a single input, GNU wc uses a minimum field width that depends on a few factors. Let me implement this matching GNU behavior.\n\nGNU wc behavior:\n- For single input: minimum width = 1 (no leading spaces for single-digit counts), but actually GNU wc uses a heuristic based on file size for the minimum width. For stdin, it's typically width 1.\n- Actually, GNU wc sets `number_width` = 1 for stdin, and for files it uses the file size to estimate the width. For simplicity and to match GNU output, I need to be careful here.\n\nLet me look at GNU wc source behavior more carefully. GNU wc:\n- For each file, it computes the number width based on the total file size\n- For multiple files, it uses the max width across all files\n- The minimum width is 1\n\nFor the task scope (R1-R5 in the task description), I need core counting. The PRD has more features like `-m`, `-L`, `--total`, `--files0-from`. Since the task says \"Implement cmd/wc core counting (-l, -w, -c)\", but the PRD covers more, I should implement the full PRD to pass differential tests.\n\nLet me implement the full wc utility:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":193,"cache_read_input_tokens":90656,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":193,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"343fd1c1-e462-4614-a39e-fffa4b487ce0","uuid":"a9081d27-8a2b-4724-9e62-5095bbdd3b22"}
