{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_016BnkCJDZ7L769XBG6zQ44y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Hmm, there's an issue - when a file is missing, I'm still printing a line with zero counts for the missing file. GNU wc does NOT print a line for the missing file - it just prints the error to stderr and continues. Let me also check the exit code issue - it seems like EXIT is empty because os.Exit is being called.\n\nAlso, I should not print the zero-count line for a failed file. Let me look at GNU wc behavior: when a file can't be opened, GNU wc prints the error to stderr but does NOT print a zero-count line for that file. However, it still includes zero in the total.\n\nWait, actually, GNU wc behavior when a file doesn't exist:\n\n\n- It prints the error to stderr for the missing file\n- It doesn't output a line for that file\n- It only prints a total line if there are 2 or more file arguments, regardless of whether some failed\n- The total should only include counts from the files that were successfully processed\n\nSo I need to fix this by not printing output lines for files that fail to open, and only printing the total when there are multiple arguments.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":184,"cache_read_input_tokens":99908,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":184,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"343fd1c1-e462-4614-a39e-fffa4b487ce0","uuid":"758b4e6f-88da-4131-a0b0-eb3bbb3c9719"}
